/* Deep lessons — Dynamic programming (dynamic-programming).
 *
 * DP is the section learners most often "know" without being able to use.
 * The reason is that most explanations teach the SOLUTIONS — knapsack, LIS,
 * edit distance — as separate recipes to memorise, when the only transferable
 * skill is the process that produces them: name the state, prove it is
 * enough, write the transition, fix the order, check the base.
 *
 * So this track spends its first seven stages on that process and treats the
 * famous problems that follow as places to run it. The late stages add the
 * shapes the process alone does not suggest: digits, expectations, and
 * getting the actual answer back out of the table.
 *
 * Original text and diagrams. Nothing copied from any source.
 */

import type { DeepLesson } from "../deep-lesson";

